<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>SecureMailScope — {{ r.capture.filename }}</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --paper:#ECEEF0; --surface:#FBFCFC; --surface-2:#F3F5F6; --surface-3:#E4E8EA;
    --ink:#0E1719; --ink-2:#47585D; --ink-3:#71838A; --line:#D2D8DA; --line-2:#BCC5C8;
    --accent:#005E6B; --accent-soft:#DCEAEC;
    --crit:#A82018; --crit-soft:#F6E2E0; --high:#9A5A00; --high-soft:#F7EBD8;
    --med:#7A5C00; --med-soft:#F6F0DC; --ok:#186047; --ok-soft:#DEEDE6;
    --info:#25467F; --info-soft:#E1E7F3;
    --mono:ui-monospace,"SF Mono",Menlo,Consolas,monospace;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
    :root{
      --paper:#0C1315; --surface:#141F22; --surface-2:#18262A; --surface-3:#223338;
      --ink:#E3EAEB; --ink-2:#9FB2B7; --ink-3:#7B8F95; --line:#28393E; --line-2:#384E54;
      --accent:#4FC4D2; --accent-soft:#12333A;
      --crit:#F08279; --crit-soft:#33191A; --high:#E3A653; --high-soft:#312414;
      --med:#D7C169; --med-soft:#2C2814; --ok:#63C9A2; --ok-soft:#122E26;
      --info:#8AAAE5; --info-soft:#17233B;
    }
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);
       font:15px/1.6 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;}
  .wrap{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:32px 24px 80px;}
  header{border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);padding-bottom:24px;margin-bottom:8px;}
  .eyebrow{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;
           color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:10px;}
  h1{font-size:30px;margin:0 0 6px;letter-spacing:-.02em;}
  h2{font-size:20px;margin:44px 0 14px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);letter-spacing:-.01em;}
  h3{font-size:15px;margin:24px 0 8px;}
  .sub{color:var(--ink-2);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;word-break:break-all;}
  .hero{display:flex;gap:26px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:26px 0;}
  .stamp{width:96px;height:96px;border-radius:6px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
         font-size:44px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;letter-spacing:-.02em;flex:none;}
  .g-A,.g-Aplus{background:var(--ok)} .g-B{background:#2E7D5B} .g-C{background:var(--high)}
  .g-D{background:#8A4A10} .g-E{background:#94301F} .g-F{background:var(--crit)}
  .kpis{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(120px,1fr));gap:12px;flex:1;min-width:280px;}
  .kpi{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;padding:12px 14px;}
  .kpi b{display:block;font-size:24px;line-height:1.1;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}
  .kpi span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);}
  table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13.5px;}
  .tw{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;background:var(--surface);margin:14px 0;}
  th{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;text-align:left;
     color:var(--ink-3);padding:10px 13px;background:var(--surface-2);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2);white-space:nowrap;}
  td{padding:9px 13px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;}
  tbody tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none}
  .mono{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;}
  .pill{display:inline-block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;
        padding:2px 7px;border-radius:3px;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;}
  .s-critical{background:var(--crit-soft);color:var(--crit)}
  .s-high{background:var(--high-soft);color:var(--high)}
  .s-medium{background:var(--med-soft);color:var(--med)}
  .s-low{background:var(--surface-3);color:var(--ink-2)}
  .s-info{background:var(--info-soft);color:var(--info)}
  .card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;padding:18px 20px;margin:12px 0;}
  .finding{border-left:3px solid var(--line-2);padding:10px 0 10px 14px;margin:12px 0;}
  .finding.critical{border-left-color:var(--crit)} .finding.high{border-left-color:var(--high)}
  .finding.medium{border-left-color:var(--med)} .finding.low{border-left-color:var(--line-2)}
  .finding.info{border-left-color:var(--info)}
  .finding .ft{font-weight:600;}
  .finding .fm{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-3);margin-top:3px;}
  .finding .fd{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:14px;margin-top:5px;}
  .finding .fr{font-size:13.5px;margin-top:6px;padding:8px 11px;background:var(--surface-2);
               border-radius:4px;border:1px solid var(--line);}
  .ev-box{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--line);
          border-radius:4px;padding:10px 12px;margin-top:6px;white-space:pre-wrap;}
  .ev-label{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;
            color:var(--ink-3);margin-bottom:4px;}
  .state-flow{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;background:var(--surface-2);
              border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:12px 14px;margin:8px 0;white-space:pre-wrap;}
  .sec-trans{color:var(--crit);font-weight:600;}
  .obs-stat{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;
            padding:2px 6px;border-radius:3px;}
  .obs-observed{background:var(--ok-soft);color:var(--ok)}
  .obs-inferred{background:var(--high-soft);color:var(--high)}
  .obs-not-observable{background:var(--surface-3);color:var(--ink-2)}
  .obs-contradicted{background:var(--crit-soft);color:var(--crit)}
  .obs-insufficient{background:var(--med-soft);color:var(--med)}
  pre{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.55;background:var(--surface-2);
      border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;padding:14px 16px;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre;}
  .note{border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--high);background:var(--high-soft);
        padding:12px 16px;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0;margin:14px 0;font-size:14px;}
  .shap{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:3px 0;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;}
  .shap .bar{height:9px;border-radius:2px;}
  .shap .pos{background:var(--crit)} .shap .neg{background:var(--ok)}
  .shap .nm{min-width:170px;color:var(--ink-2)}
  .muted{color:var(--ink-3);font-size:13px;}
  footer{margin-top:60px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);
         font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-3);line-height:1.7;}
  @media print{
    body{background:#fff;color:#000}
    .wrap{max-width:none;padding:0}
    h2{page-break-after:avoid} .card,.finding{page-break-inside:avoid}
    @page{margin:16mm;}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <div class="eyebrow">SecureMailScope · Forensic Report · PS 26159</div>
  <h1>Cryptographic posture assessment</h1>
  <div class="sub">
    {{ r.capture.filename }} · {{ r.capture.format }} · {{ '{:,}'.format(r.capture.bytes) }} bytes ·
    {{ r.capture.packet_count }} packets<br>
    SHA-256 {{ r.capture.sha256 }}<br>
    Captured {{ r.capture.first_packet_time or 'unknown' }} · Report generated {{ r.generated_at }}
  </div>
</header>
{% if r.coverage %}
<section><h2>Evidence coverage</h2><p>{{ r.coverage.assessed_checks }} / {{ r.coverage.applicable_checks }} applicable checks assessed; {{ r.coverage.limited_sessions }} sessions have visibility limits. Coverage is separate from the grade. Unobservable evidence has not been verified.</p></section>
{% endif %}
{% if r.provenance %}
<details><summary>Analysis provenance</summary><dl>{% for key in r.provenance %}<dt>{{ key }}</dt><dd class="sub">{{ r.provenance[key] }}</dd>{% endfor %}</dl></details>
{% endif %}
{% if r.history and r.history.servers %}
<section><h2>Historical observations</h2><p>Deviations are review prompts, not proof of an attack. Missing findings are not proof of remediation.</p>
{% for server in r.history.servers %}<div class="card"><b>{{ server.host }}:{{ server.port }}</b> · {{ server.status }}<p>{{ server.prior_sessions }} prior sessions in {{ server.prior_captures }} distinct captures. {{ server.identity_confidence }}</p>
{% for change in server.changes %}<p>{{ change.field }}: {{ change.previous|join(', ') }} → {{ change.new|join(', ') }}</p>{% endfor %}
{% for anomaly in server.anomalies %}{% if anomaly.unusual %}<p>Unusual session {{ anomaly.session_id }} · score {{ anomaly.score }}</p>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</div>{% endfor %}</section>
{% endif %}


<div class="hero">
  <div class="stamp g-{{ 'Aplus' if r.overall_grade == 'A+' else r.overall_grade }}">{{ r.overall_grade }}</div>
  <div class="kpis">
    <div class="kpi"><b>{{ r.counts.sessions }}</b><span>Sessions</span></div>
    <div class="kpi"><b>{{ r.counts.assets }}</b><span>Servers</span></div>
    <div class="kpi"><b>{{ r.counts.critical }}</b><span>Critical</span></div>
    <div class="kpi"><b>{{ r.counts.high }}</b><span>High</span></div>
    <div class="kpi"><b>{{ r.counts.credentials_exposed }}</b><span>Creds exposed</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

{% if r.warnings %}
{% for w in r.warnings %}<div class="note"><b>Capture note.</b> {{ w }}</div>{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<h2>1 · Servers, worst first</h2>
<div class="tw"><table>
  <thead><tr>
    <th>Server</th><th>Proto</th><th>Role</th><th>Grade</th><th class="mono">Raw</th>
    <th>TLS seen</th><th>Sessions</th><th>Exposure</th><th>Capped by</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for a in r.assets %}
    <tr>
      <td class="mono">{{ a.host }}:{{ a.port }}</td>
      <td>{{ a.protocol }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ a.role }}</td>
      <td><span class="pill s-{{ 'critical' if a.grade.letter in ['F','E'] else 'high' if a.grade.letter in ['D','C'] else 'info' }}">{{ a.grade.letter }}</span>
          {% if not a.grade.trusted %}<span class="pill s-low">untrusted</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ a.grade.raw_score }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{% if a.best_tls %}{{ a.worst_tls }}{% if a.version_spread %} → {{ a.best_tls }}{% endif %}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ a.session_count }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ a.exposure_score }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ a.grade.capped_by or '—' }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2>2 · Prioritised remediation</h2>
{% if r.remediation %}
<div class="tw"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Severity</th><th>Rule</th><th>Action</th><th>Servers</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for m in r.remediation %}
    <tr>
      <td class="mono">{{ m.order }}</td>
      <td><span class="pill s-{{ m.severity }}">{{ m.severity }}</span></td>
      <td class="mono">{{ m.rule_id }}<br><span class="muted">{{ m.standard }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ m.title }}<br><span class="muted">{{ m.action }}</span></td>
      <td class="mono">{{ m.affected_assets|join(', ') }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% else %}<p class="muted">No actionable findings.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>3 · Session detail</h2>
{% for s in r.sessions %}
<div class="card">
  <h3>Session #{{ s.tcp_stream }} · {{ s.protocol|upper }} over {{ s.tls_mode }}
      <span class="pill s-{{ 'critical' if s.grade.letter in ['F','E'] else 'high' if s.grade.letter in ['D','C'] else 'info' }}">{{ s.grade.letter }}</span></h3>
  {% if s.coverage %}<p>Coverage: {{ s.coverage.assessed_checks }} / {{ s.coverage.applicable_checks }} applicable checks. Not assessed: {{ s.coverage.skipped_checks|join(', ') or 'none' }}.</p>{% endif %}
  <div class="sub">
    {{ s.client.ip }}:{{ s.client.port }} → {{ s.server.ip }}:{{ s.server.port }}
    · frames {{ s.first_frame }}–{{ s.last_frame }} · {{ s.duration_seconds }}s
    · role {{ s.role }} · confidence {{ s.confidence }}
  </div>

  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th colspan="2">TLS handshake</th><th colspan="2">X.509 certificate</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="mono">Version</td><td class="mono">{{ s.tls_version or 'none — cleartext' }}</td>
        <td class="mono">Visibility</td><td class="mono">{{ s.cert_visibility }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="mono">Cipher</td><td class="mono">{{ s.cipher_suite or '—' }}</td>
        <td class="mono">Subject</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ s.chain[0].subject if s.chain else '—' }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="mono">Key exchange</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ s.kex or '—' }}{% if s.kex_bits %} · {{ s.kex_bits }}-bit equiv{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="mono">Issuer</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ s.chain[0].issuer if s.chain else '—' }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="mono">Forward secrecy</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ 'yes' if s.forward_secrecy else 'no' if s.forward_secrecy is not none else '—' }}</td>
        <td class="mono">Valid until</td>
        <td class="mono">{% if s.chain %}{{ s.chain[0].not_after }}
            {% if s.chain[0].expired_at_capture %}<span class="pill s-critical">expired at capture</span>
            {% else %}<span class="pill s-info">valid at capture</span>{% endif %}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="mono">JA4 / JA3</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ s.ja4 or '—' }}<br>{{ s.ja3 or '' }}</td>
        <td class="mono">Key / signature</td>
        <td class="mono">{% if s.chain %}{{ s.chain[0].key_algorithm }} {{ s.chain[0].key_bits }} · {{ s.chain[0].signature_hash }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="mono">STARTTLS</td>
        <td class="mono">offered {{ s.starttls_offered }} · requested {{ s.starttls_requested }} · completed {{ s.starttls_accepted }}</td>
        <td class="mono">Chain / revocation</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ s.chain_valid if s.chain_valid is not none else 'not evaluated' }} · {{ s.revocation }}</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <div class="mono muted">
    Grade {{ s.grade.letter }} — weighted {{ s.grade.raw_score }}
    (protocol {{ '%.0f'|format(s.grade.components.protocol) }} ·
     key exchange {{ '%.0f'|format(s.grade.components.key_exchange) }} ·
     cipher {{ '%.0f'|format(s.grade.components.cipher) }})
    {%- if s.grade.capped_by %}, capped to {{ s.grade.letter }} by {{ s.grade.capped_by }}{% endif %}
    {%- if s.grade.zero_category %}; zero in {{ s.grade.zero_category }} forces the score to 0{% endif %}.
  </div>

  {% if s.capability_mangled %}
  <div class="note">
    <b>Downgrade evidence.</b> The capability list contains
    <code class="mono">{{ s.mangled_token }}</code> where the STARTTLS keyword belongs — the same
    equal-length substitution measured in the wild by Durumeric et al., IMC 2015.
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if s.cleartext_auth %}
  <div class="note">
    <b>Credentials exposed.</b> {{ s.cleartext_auth.mechanism }} authentication for
    <code class="mono">{{ s.cleartext_auth.username or 'unknown user' }}</code> was sent before any
    encryption existed (frame {{ s.cleartext_auth.frame }}). The secret itself is not stored in this
    report; SHA-256 <code class="mono">{{ s.cleartext_auth.secret_sha256[:24] }}…</code> is retained
    so reuse can be correlated. Treat this credential as compromised.
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% for f in s.findings %}
  <div class="finding {{ f.severity }}">
    <div class="ft"><span class="pill s-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity }}</span> {{ f.rule_id }} — {{ f.title }}</div>
    <div class="fm">{{ f.standard }} · frames {{ f.evidence.frames|join(', ') }} · stream {{ f.evidence.tcp_stream }}{% if f.standards_refs %} · standards {{ f.standards_refs|join(', ') }}{% endif %}</div>
    {% if f.detail %}<div class="fd">{{ f.detail }}</div>{% endif %}
    <div class="fr"><b>Fix:</b> {{ f.remediation }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

  {# Phase 2: Evidence section per session #}
  {% if r.email_security_state_machines %}
  {% for sm in r.email_security_state_machines %}
  {% if sm.session_id == s.session_id %}
  <h3>Email security state machine</h3>
  <div class="state-flow">
{% for st in sm.states %}{{ st.name }}{% if not loop.last %} → {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% if sm.security_relevant_transitions %}
  <div class="ev-label">Security-relevant transitions</div>
  {% for tr in sm.security_relevant_transitions %}
  <div class="finding high">
    <div class="ft"><span class="pill s-high">security</span> {{ tr.from_state }} → {{ tr.to_state }}</div>
    {% if tr.details %}<div class="fd">{{ tr.details }}</div>{% endif %}
    <div class="fm">Frame {{ tr.frame or 'unknown' }} · confidence {{ tr.confidence }} · status <span class="obs-stat obs-{{ tr.status }}">{{ tr.status }}</span> · frame precision {{ tr.frame_precision or 'UNKNOWN' }}</div>
    {% if tr.observation_refs %}
    <div class="ev-box">
{% for ref in tr.observation_refs %}<span class="obs-stat obs-{{ ref.status }}">{{ ref.status }}</span> {{ ref.observation_type }}{% if ref.excerpt %}: {{ ref.excerpt[:100] }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if sm.limitations %}
  <div class="ev-label">Limitations</div>
  <ul class="muted">
    {% for lim in sm.limitations %}<li>{{ lim }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
  {# Phase 3: Security Controls #}
  {% if s.security_controls %}
  <h3>Security controls</h3>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Status</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for c in s.security_controls %}
    <tr>
      <td class="mono">{{ c.control_id }}</td>
      <td><span class="pill s-{% if c.status == 'FAIL' %}critical{% elif c.status == 'WARN' %}high{% elif c.status == 'PASS' %}info{% else %}low{% endif %}">{{ c.status }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ c.reason }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  {% endif %}

  {# Phase 3: Reasoning #}
  {% if s.reasoning %}
  <h3>Security reasoning</h3>
  {% for r in s.reasoning %}
  <div class="finding high">
    <div class="ft"><span class="pill s-high">reasoning</span> {{ r.rule_id }}</div>
    {% if r.observed_facts %}
    <div class="ev-label">Observed facts</div>
    <ul class="muted">
      {% for f in r.observed_facts %}
      <li>{{ f.description }} <span class="obs-stat obs-{{ f.status }}">{{ f.status }}</span></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if r.inferences %}
    <div class="ev-label">Inferences</div>
    <ul class="muted">
      {% for i in r.inferences %}
      <li>{{ i.description }} (confidence: {{ i.confidence }})</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if r.possible_explanations %}
    <div class="ev-label">Possible explanations</div>
    <ul class="muted">
      {% for e in r.possible_explanations %}
      <li><b>{{ e.explanation_id }}</b> — {{ e.description }}
        <span class="pill s-{% if e.status == 'likely' %}critical{% elif e.status == 'possible' %}high{% else %}low{% endif %}">{{ e.confidence }}</span>
        {% if e.supporting_evidence %}<br><span class="mono muted">+ {{ e.supporting_evidence|length }} supporting</span>{% endif %}
        {% if e.contradicting_evidence %}<br><span class="mono muted">— {{ e.contradicting_evidence|length }} contradicting</span>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="fm">Overall confidence: {{ r.confidence }} · Risk: {{ r.risk.overall if r.risk else 'unknown' }} (impact {{ r.risk.impact.value if r.risk else '—' }}, exposure {{ r.risk.exposure.value if r.risk else '—' }})</div>
    {% if r.limitations %}
    <div class="ev-label">Limitations</div>
    <ul class="muted">{% for l in r.limitations %}<li>{{ l }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if s.ml %}
  <h3>Model assessment</h3>
  <div class="mono muted">
    posture {{ s.ml.risk_class }} · P(critical) {{ s.ml.risk_score }} ·
    anomaly {{ 'yes' if s.ml.anomaly else 'no' }}
    {%- if s.ml.anomaly_score is not none %} ({{ s.ml.anomaly_score }}){% endif %}
    · model {{ s.ml.model_version }}
  </div>
  <p class="fd">{{ s.ml.explanation }}</p>
  {% if s.ml.shap %}
  <div>
    {% for c in s.ml.shap[:8] %}
    <div class="shap">
      <span class="nm">{{ c.feature }} = {{ c.value }}</span>
      <span class="bar {{ 'pos' if c.contribution > 0 else 'neg' }}"
            style="width:{{ (c.contribution|abs * 260)|round|int if (c.contribution|abs * 260) < 260 else 260 }}px"></span>
      <span>{{ '%+.4f'|format(c.contribution) }}</span>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="muted">TreeSHAP contributions toward the predicted class. Positive values push the
     session toward that verdict; negative values pull away from it.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if s.command_transcript %}
  <h3>Reconstructed transcript (cleartext phase)</h3>
  <pre>{% for line in s.command_transcript[:24] %}{{ line }}
{% endfor %}</pre>
  {% endif %}

  {% if s.notes %}<p class="muted">{% for n in s.notes %}{{ n }} {% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}

{# Phase 3: Cross-session patterns #}
{% if r.cross_session_patterns %}
<h2>5 · Cross-session patterns</h2>
<p class="muted">Patterns are signals to review — they do not confirm attacks. Each
pattern lists confidence and possible interpretations.</p>
{% for p in r.cross_session_patterns %}
<div class="card">
  <b>{{ p.name }}</b> · <span class="pill s-{{ 'high' if p.confidence == 'high' else 'med' if p.confidence == 'medium' else 'low' }}">{{ p.confidence }}</span>
  <p>{{ p.description }}</p>
  {% if p.observations %}
  <div class="ev-label">Observations</div>
  <ul class="muted">{% for o in p.observations %}<li>{{ o }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% if p.possible_interpretations %}
  <div class="ev-label">Possible interpretations</div>
  <ul class="muted">{% for i in p.possible_interpretations %}<li>{{ i }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% if p.limitations %}
  <div class="ev-label">Limitations</div>
  <ul class="muted">{% for l in p.limitations %}<li>{{ l }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% if p.standards %}
  <div class="mono muted">Standards: {{ p.standards|join(', ') }}</div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<h2>4 · Scope and limitations</h2>
<div class="card">
  <ul>
    <li><b>Passive analysis only.</b> No packet was ever transmitted and no server was contacted.
        Every statement above derives from the capture file whose SHA-256 is printed on page one.</li>
    <li><b>Grades are scoped to observed sessions.</b> An active scanner probes every option a
        server supports; a passive tool sees only what was actually negotiated. Server-level grades
        combine the best and worst observation, following the published Qualys methodology, but they
        do not describe the server's full capability surface.</li>
    <li><b>Certificate validity is judged against the capture clock</b>, not today's date — so a
        certificate that was valid when recorded is not reported as expired.</li>
    <li><b>TLS 1.3 encrypts the Certificate message</b> (RFC 8446 §4.4). Sessions marked
        <span class="mono">encrypted_tls13</span> carry no certificate findings; that is a property
        of the protocol, not an omission.</li>
    <li><b>Revocation</b> is only checked where the server stapled an OCSP response. Offline there is
        no responder to query, and unchecked is reported as <span class="mono">unknown_offline</span>
        rather than assumed good.</li>
    <li><b>The model never decides a verdict.</b> All findings above come from the deterministic rule
        engine. Model output is advisory: prioritisation and anomaly surfacing.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<footer>
  SecureMailScope {{ r.tool_version }} · schema {{ r.schema_version }} · Smart India Hackathon 2026 ·
  Problem Statement 26159 · NTRO<br>
  Evidence hash SHA-256 {{ r.capture.sha256 }}
</footer>

</div>

<script>
/*
 * "Save as PDF" opens this report with ?print=1 and the browser does the
 * rendering. That is the whole PDF feature.
 *
 * It used to be a server-side render through WeasyPrint, which needs Pango and
 * cairo — native libraries that install cleanly in a Debian container and often
 * not at all on a Mac. So the endpoint returned 501 everywhere it was actually
 * used, behind a <a download> link that discards error bodies, and the button
 * failed with "this site can't be reached" and no explanation. Printing the
 * page uses the @page rules already in this stylesheet, produces the same
 * document, needs nothing installed, and behaves identically in every
 * deployment.
 *
 * Gated on the query string so a saved copy of this file never prints itself
 * when someone opens it.
 */
(function () {
  try {
    if (new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('print') === '1') {
      window.addEventListener('load', function () { window.print(); });
    }
  } catch (e) {
    /* Older browser without URLSearchParams: the reader can still press Ctrl-P. */
  }
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
